    "transcription": "FULLTEXT_ORIGINAL:\n[Charles's page only; the adjoining person's entry is outside this transcription. Blank form fields are shown as [blank].]\nIN THE MATTER OF THE PETITION OF\nCharles Albert Brenay\nTO BE ADMITTED A CITIZEN OF THE UNITED STATES OF AMERICA.\nFiled Oct. 24, 1919\nOATH OF ALLEGIANCE\nI hereby declare, on oath, that I absolutely and entirely renounce and abjure all allegiance and fidelity to any foreign prince, potentate,\nstate, or sovereignty, and particularly to George V the King of Great Britain & Ireland\nof whom I have heretofore been a subject; that I will support and defend the Constitution and laws of the United States of America against all\nenemies, foreign and domestic; and that I will bear true faith and allegiance to the same.\nCharles Albert Brenay\nSubscribed and sworn to before me, in open Court, this 7th day of June, A. D. 1920.\nWm. A. Harvey Jr., Clerk.\nNOTE.—In renunciation of title of nobility, add the following to the oath of allegiance before it is executed: “I further renounce the title of (give title), an order of nobility, which I have heretofore held.”\nORDER OF COURT ADMITTING PETITIONER\nUpon consideration of the petition of Charles Albert Brenay, and affidavits in support thereof, and\nfurther testimony taken in open Court, it is ordered that the said petitioner, who has taken the oath required by law, be, and hereby is, admitted\nto become a citizen of the United States of America, this 7th day of June, A. D. 1920.\n(It is further ordered, upon consideration of the petition of the said [blank], that his name be,\nand hereby is, changed to [blank], under authority of the provisions of section 6 of the act approved\nJune 29, 1906 (34 Stat. L., pt. 1, p. 596), as amended by the act approved March 4, 1913, entitled “An act to create a Department of Labor.”)\nBy the Court:\nFrank Emerick\nCircuit Judge.\nORDER OF COURT DENYING PETITION\n[This separate denial form is uncompleted.]\nUpon consideration of the petition of [blank] and the motion of\n[blank]\n[blank] for the United States in open Court this\n[blank] day of [blank], 19[blank], it appearing that [blank]\n[blank]\nTHE SAID PETITION IS HEREBY DENIED.\n[blank], J.\nMEMORANDUM OF CONTINUANCES\nREASONS FOR CONTINUANCE\nContinued from Dec. 1, 1919 — did not present\nto [blank], 19[blank]\nContinued from [blank], 19[blank]\nto [blank], 19[blank]\nNAMES OF SUBSTITUTED WITNESSES\n[blank], occupation [blank], residing at [blank]\n[blank], occupation [blank], residing at [blank]\nCertificate of Naturalization, No. 1382452, issued on the 7th day of June, A. D. 1920.\n[INSERT ON FOLLOWING LINES MARRIAGES AND BIRTHS OCCURRING AFTER PETITION AND BEFORE NATURALIZATION.]\n[Lines blank.]\n\nFULLTEXT_TRANSLATION\nNot applicable — the original is in English."
